          "timing": "/lessons/exponential-graphs-am/scene-01-b18.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "Three times something is zero only if E to the power two X is zero. But a power of E is never zero.",
          "asks": ["Why can we divide by 3?", "Why is e to a power never zero?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "se", "on": "only if E" },
            { "do": "note", "text": "e to any power is never zero", "near": "se", "on": "never zero" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/exponential-graphs-am/scene-01-b19.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/exponential-graphs-am/scene-01-b19.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "So there are no solutions, and no X intercept. The curve never meets the X axis.",
          "asks": ["Does no solutions mean I made a mistake?"],
          "aside": {
            "text": "Why is it never zero?",
            "slug": "indices-exponential-never-zero",
            "read": [
              "$e$ is a positive number, about $2.718$.",
              "A positive number to any power is still positive.",
              "So $e^{2x} > 0$ for every $x$.",
              "It can get very close to $0$, but never reach it.",
              "**So $e^{2x} = 0$ has no solutions: the curve never meets the $x$-axis.**"
            ]
          },
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "ns", "on": "no solutions" },
            { "do": "mark", "kind": "box", "token": "ns", "on": "no X intercept" }
